---
title: "Case study hero"
eyebrow: "Components"
lead: "The opening of a case study page: a back button, an eyebrow, a title, a subtitle, optional buttons and a 16:9 image. Two tones (plain or a blue band) and, on desktop, two layouts (image below or beside the text)."
permalink: /components/case-study-hero/
---
{% from "components.njk" import button %}
<section aria-labelledby="demo-h">
  <h2 id="demo-h" class="type-h2">Case study hero</h2>
  <p>A tertiary back button comes first, then the text and a 16:9 image. The text has an eyebrow, the page's one <code>h1</code>, a subtitle and up to a few secondary buttons that open in a new tab. The hero has two settings. <strong>Tone</strong> is plain (the default, on the page surface) or band (a blue band). <strong>Layout</strong> is below (the default) or beside. Beside works on desktop only; tablet and mobile always put the image below the text. The text and image in the demos are placeholders.</p>
  <h3 class="type-h3">Plain tone, image below</h3>
  {% demo "Case study hero, plain tone, image below, with placeholder text and image", "block" %}
  <header class="cs-hero">
    <div class="cs-hero__back">
      {{ button("All work", type="tertiary", href="#", icon="arrow_back", iconPosition="leading") }}
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero__band">
      <div class="cs-hero__text">
        <div class="cs-hero__heading">
          <p class="cs-hero__eyebrow type-label">Project type, Role</p>
          <p class="cs-hero__title type-h1">Case study title</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-hero__lede">
          <p class="cs-hero__subtitle type-lead">One or two sentences that say what the project was and what changed.</p>
          <div class="cs-hero__actions">
            {{ button("Link label", type="secondary", href="#", icon="open_in_new", iconPosition="trailing", external=true) }}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-hero__image">
        <div class="placeholder-image"><p class="type-small">Placeholder image, 16:9</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  {% enddemo %}
  <h3 class="type-h3">Band tone, image below</h3>
  {% demo "Case study hero, band tone, image below, with placeholder text and image", "block" %}
  <header class="cs-hero cs-hero--band">
    <div class="cs-hero__back">
      {{ button("All work", type="tertiary", href="#", icon="arrow_back", iconPosition="leading") }}
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero__band">
      <div class="cs-hero__text">
        <div class="cs-hero__heading">
          <p class="cs-hero__eyebrow type-label">Project type, Role</p>
          <p class="cs-hero__title type-h1">Case study title</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-hero__lede">
          <p class="cs-hero__subtitle type-lead">One or two sentences that say what the project was and what changed.</p>
          <div class="cs-hero__actions">
            {{ button("Link label", type="secondary", onBrand=true, href="#", icon="open_in_new", iconPosition="trailing", external=true) }}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-hero__image">
        <div class="placeholder-image"><p class="type-small">Placeholder image, 16:9</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  {% enddemo %}
  <h3 class="type-h3">Band tone, image beside (desktop)</h3>
  <p>Below 1024px this one looks like the one above. Widen the window to see the image move beside the text.</p>
  {% demo "Case study hero, band tone, image beside the text on desktop, with placeholder text and image", "block" %}
  <header class="cs-hero cs-hero--band cs-hero--beside">
    <div class="cs-hero__back">
      {{ button("All work", type="tertiary", href="#", icon="arrow_back", iconPosition="leading") }}
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero__band">
